BUG: PATCH /api/quotations/{id} wipes client. RCA: In /app/backend/quotation_routes.py::_compute_and_pack, the block:
    client_id, client = await inv_routes._client_snapshot(studio_id, data.get('client_id'), client_override)
is executed unconditionally on every partial update. When the frontend sends {"subject":"…"} only, `data.get('client_id')` and `client_override` are both None, so _client_snapshot returns its 'no info' default (name='Client', everything else None), which is then persisted via the $set update. Reproduction (curl): create with client.name='REPRO_CLIENT' -> PATCH {"subject":"patched"} -> GET returns client.name='Client'. Mitigation: in _compute_and_pack, only recompute the client when the PATCH explicitly provides client_id or client; otherwise reuse existing['client_id']/existing['client']. Pseudocode:
    if data.get('client') is not None or data.get('client_id') is not None:
        client_id, client = await inv_routes._client_snapshot(...)
    else:
        client_id = (existing or {}).get('client_id')
        client = (existing or {}).get('client') or {}
